{"availability":"available","full":"dhilt/vscroll","name":"vscroll","description":"A JavaScript Virtual Scroll Engine","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":45,"forks":3,"created":"2020-12-30T02:35:23Z","updated":"2026-10-07T15:01:12Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dhilt.github.io/vscroll/","topics":["infinite-scroll","javascript","typescript","virtual-list","virtual-scroll","virtual-scroller","virtual-scrolling","virtualization","virtualscroll"],"demo":"https://dhilt.github.io/vscroll/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.188Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.188Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.188Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.188Z","stars":45,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A framework-independent virtual scrolling engine for JavaScript and TypeScript.","Virtual scrolling is a technique for displaying large lists efficiently. Instead of rendering every item at once, it keeps a small set of items in the DOM — those in and around the visible area — and updates that set as the user scrolls. This reduces DOM size and rendering work while preserving a familiar scrolling experience.","VScroll provides a framework-independent core engine for virtual scrolling. An application can use it directly or through a platform-specific wrapper called a consumer. The diagram shows how the engine reaches the end user when a consumer is used."],"features":["ngx-ui-scroll — an Angular virtual scrolling directive.","vscroll-native — a virtual scrolling module for native JavaScript applications.","Vue integration sample — an example of using VScroll in Vue."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dhilt/vscroll/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"156d134268ffe8b577f8695910e33db09f7be1a07c065341b089b5d84e936a78","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.307Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T18:43:27.307Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text"